; IR-agnostic. Knows about bytes, pointers, PTX strings and kernel handles;
; never about Graph or Kernel_ir. The real implementation wraps cudajit
; (driver API + NVRTC). Until then every function raises, so the rest of
; the project builds and tests on a machine with no GPU.
(library
 (name cudacaml_runtime)
 (public_name cudacaml.runtime)
 ; [ctypes] and [ctypes.foreign] are for lib/runtime/pinned.ml, which binds
 ; cuMemHostAlloc / cuMemFreeHost by hand: cudajit 0.7 does not expose them.
 ; Both already come in with cudajit, so this adds no opam dependency.
 (libraries cudacaml_ir cudajit.cuda cudajit.nvrtc ctypes ctypes.foreign))
